-<section class="product-content-band"><div class="container"><div class="row g-5"><div class="col-lg-7 content-copy"><h2 class="section-title">Surety Bonds and Trusts that gets it right</h2><h2 class="section-title mt-4">Bonds and trusts</h2><p>BMC-84 bonds, often known as BMC-84 bonds, are surety bonds required by the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration to help protect shippers and carriers from non-payment or fraudulent activity.</p><p>A BMC-85 trust can also satisfy financial responsibility requirements by placing funds into a dedicated trust account.</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4">The role of trust in transportation compliance</h2><p>A BMC-85 trust generally ties up capital that could otherwise support marketing, technology, hiring, or growth. For many smaller companies, that liquidity tradeoff matters.</p><p>A surety bond may provide a different path to compliance, with premium costs affected by creditworthiness and other risk factors.</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4">Choosing the right provider</h2><p>Bond and trust providers should be financially sound, responsive, and experienced with transportation claims and compliance.</p><p>Motive helps trucking and transportation businesses review options and maintain the financial protection needed to operate confidently.</p></div><div class="col-lg-5"><div class="coverage-panel sticky-lg-top"><h3>Coverage highlights</h3><ul class="coverage-list"><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>BMC-84 surety bonds</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>BMC-85 trust guidance</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>BMC-84 bonds</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>Financial responsibility review</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>Transportation compliance support</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>Renewal and maintenance guidance</span></li></ul><a class="btn btn-start w-100 mt-3" href="contact-us.html#contactForm">Get Your Quote -&gt;</a></div></div></div></div></section>
+<section class="product-content-band"><div class="container"><div class="row g-5"><div class="col-lg-7 content-copy"><h2 class="section-title">Freight Broker Financial Responsibility</h2><h2 class="section-title mt-4">Bonds and trusts</h2><p>A BMC-84 surety bond provides financial security for payments owed to shippers or motor carriers when a broker fails to meet its covered transportation obligations. FMCSA requires property and household-goods brokers, and applicable freight forwarders, to maintain $75,000 in financial security through a BMC-84 bond or BMC-85 trust.</p><p>A BMC-85 is a trust arrangement with an eligible financial institution. It must hold $75,000 in qualifying assets; a trust administration fee is not a substitute for those assets. The provider files the appropriate bond or trust form with FMCSA.</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4">The role of trust in transportation compliance</h2><p>Compare the funding obligations as well as the fees. A BMC-85 commits qualifying assets to the trust, which can affect the funds available to run the business.</p><p>With a BMC-84, an approved applicant generally pays a premium rather than depositing the full bond amount. Underwriting may also require collateral. Review indemnity and reimbursement terms: paying a premium does not eliminate the broker's obligations for covered claims.</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4">January 16, 2026 FMCSA changes</h2><p>The 2026 rules tightened trust asset and provider standards. BMC-85 assets are limited to cash, irrevocable letters of credit from federally insured depository institutions, and U.S. Treasury bonds, and must be convertible to cash within seven calendar days. Loan and finance companies are no longer eligible BMC-85 trustees.</p><p>The rules also address provider reporting, financial failure and suspension when available security falls below $75,000. Respond promptly to any FMCSA notice and follow the current regulatory procedures. These changes did not replace the $75,000 security requirement.</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4">Choosing the right provider</h2><p>Bond and trust providers should be financially sound, responsive, and experienced with transportation claims and compliance.</p><p>Motive helps brokers and transportation businesses review available options. For a side-by-side comparison, read our <a href="bmc-84-vs-bmc-85.html">BMC-84 bond vs. BMC-85 trust guide</a>.</p><p>Reviewed November 10, 2026. Sources: <a href="https://www.fmcsa.dot.gov/registration/broker-and-freight-forwarder-financial-responsibility-rule-overview-and-compliance" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FMCSA rule overview</a>, <a href="https://www.fmcsa.dot.gov/registration/insurance-filing-requirements" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FMCSA filing requirements</a>, and <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-49/subtitle-B/chapter-III/subchapter-B/part-387/subpart-C/section-387.307" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">current 49 CFR 387.307</a>.</p></div><div class="col-lg-5"><div class="coverage-panel sticky-lg-top"><h3>Coverage highlights</h3><ul class="coverage-list"><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>BMC-84 surety bonds</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>BMC-85 trust guidance</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>Financial responsibility review</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>Transportation compliance support</span></li><li><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i><span>Renewal and maintenance guidance</span></li></ul><a class="btn btn-start w-100 mt-3" href="contact-us.html#contactForm">Get Your Quote -&gt;</a></div></div></div></div></section>
